Watch the effects of optimizing the hierarchy of the animatable object in the dialog Show Graphic
Structure [button].
Note
As you cannot restore discarded data, only flatten the structure after you are done with modeling the
object! You will not detect any difference in the appearance of the object; you will see a difference
though in its graphic structure, which Plant Simulation flattened for better performance at runtime.
Only accept the result, when the optimized graphic meets your intentions in its looks and in its structure.
Back to Visualizing the Material Flow
Optimizing the Model
After we created our model and are sure that we do not have to make any more changes, we can optimize
it.
Note
As you cannot restore discarded data, we advise to optimize the model only after you finished creating it.
Optimizing the model improves performance.
We also recommend to save the model under a different name before optimizing it. This way you can
return to the state the model had before optimizing it in case the optimized model reports errors or does
not meet you expectations.
Proceed as follows:
• Save the model with a new name before optimizing it. This way you can return to the state the model
had before optimizing it in case the optimized model reports errors or does not meet you expectations.
• Click Optimize Model 
  on the Home ribbon tab.
• Select which optimization you want to execute. You can either choose only a single setting or any
combination of the provided settings.
Below we demonstrate the effects of the individual settings with our model
MyTurnplateShrinkwrapper3D.spp.
Optimizing the Model
10-1150 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

The finished model originally has this size.
◦ First, we only select the setting Clean Up Class Library. This removes object classes from the Class
Library that are not used in the model.
This setting reduces the file size the most.
Optimizing the Model
Plant Simulation Help 10-1151
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

If you want to continue working with the optimized model at a later point in time, you can re-add the
missing objects with Start > Manage Class Library.
◦ Then, we only select the setting Optimize 3D Attribute Inheritance.
This setting reduces the file size in our example only marginally.
◦ Then, we only select the setting Optimize 3D Graphic Structure.
This setting reduces the file size in our example only marginally.
If you want to work with your model later on and would like to be able to edit your graphics, we
recommend to not activate Optimize 3D Graphic Structure.
◦ Finally, we combine all settings.
This results in the smallest file size which, alas, is only marginally smaller than the setting Clean up
Class Library.
Optimizing the Model
10-1152 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

