Recording a Video
Record a Video
You can record a video of the crucial parts of your simulation model. This way, you can pass the video on to
anybody or publish it on the Intranet or the Internet, without the person viewing the video having to install
Plant Simulation on his computer. The recorder creates an AVI file that any multimedia player can play.
The Video Ribbon Tab provides all tools for recording and playing the video.
Back to Visualizing the Material Flow
Select Video Settings
After you prepared the scene, you can select the video settings for recording the scene.
Proceed as follows:
Recording a Video
Plant Simulation Help 10-1153
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• Click Start Simple Recording 
  on the ribbon tab Video and select the settings to record a video of
Plant Simulation or the active 3D window.
The video will be recorded in real-time, meaning that recording a minute of physical real time
corresponds to a minute of playback time in the video. You might, for example, use this type of video
recording to demonstrate how to operate a model.
• Click Start Simulation Recording 
  on the ribbon tab Video and select the settings to record a
video of a simulation. The simulation does not have to run beforehand.
The video records in scaled simulation time, meaning that the number of minutes of simulation time,
which you entered as Real-time x [video], corresponds to one minute of playback time of the video.
You can, for example, use this type of video recording to play the simulated production with realistic
time behavior.
Select Video Settings
10-1154 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Note
To prevent that Plant Simulation overwrites the last recorded AVI file, rename the output file before
recording another video.
Back to Record a Video
Set Up the Scene for Recording
There are a number of items to keep in mind before you start recording the scene.
Proceed as follows:
• Drag the window to a size that shows all that you want to show to the viewer, but not more,
unnecessary information.
Note
If you would like to record a video in the display resolutions 720p or 1080p, you can set the size of
the window to be recorded to these sizes in the dialogs Start Simple Recording and Start Simulation
Recording.
The size of the scene determines the size of the video, a large scene uses more processor time and
might take a long time to animate and creates a larger video file.
• Decide from which position and which angle you want to view and record the scene. Then, rotate and
zoom the scene accordingly before starting the simulation.
Set Up the Scene for Recording
Plant Simulation Help 10-1155
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Note
If you are recording a simulation video, you can automatically connect the recording with playing a
camera animation by selecting Play Camera Path.
Back to Record a Video
Record the Video
After you set up the scene and selected the video settings, you can record the video by using the features
on the Video ribbon tab.
• If you do not want to record the scene from the beginning of the simulation, start the simulation and
let the animation proceed to about the time you want to start recording. Then, click 
  or 
respectively to start recording.
• If necessary, reset the simulation model by clicking 
 .
• To start the simulation, click Start 
 .
• To start recording the animation, click 
  on the Video ribbon tab.
Note
Be aware that the recorder records the contents of the currently active window. If you click into
another window during the recording session, or roll the mouse over a button to display a tooltip,
these will show up in your recorded video as well. This might ruin the effect of your recorded video.
• To cancel recording, click 
• To pause recording, click 
 . This deactivates the Pause button.
You might pause recording if you do not want to show a certain section of the animation, and start
recording the next section of interest by clicking 
  or 
  respectively again.
• To stop recording the video, click 
 .
3D show a dialog telling you that it saved the AVI file to the location and with the name you entered.
Click OK to close the dialog and to continue working.
Note
If you want to view the video after you recorded it, we recommend to stop the simulation, as it uses a
considerable amount of your computer’s resources.
