Visualizing the Simulation Model in Omniverse
Visualize the Simulation Model in Omniverse
You can visualize your Plant Simulation 2606 simulation model in NVIDIA Omniverse using the Omniverse
Connector.
The Omniverse Connector 
  is only active if you have a subscription for this optional product.
To create an excellent looking visualization of your Plant Simulation 2606 simulation model in Omniverse,
proceed as follows:
• Start the Omniverse Connector
• Set Up a New Filesystem Connection
• Establish a Live Connection to Omniverse
You can then open the project in the Live data area of the Nvidia Omniverse Composer and work on
enhancing the looks of the model.
• Use Omniverse with the Function MVA_WriteUSD
See also
Omniverse Connector
Videos
Play the Video
Plant Simulation Help 10-1157
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Start the Omniverse Connector
Start the Omniverse Connector to establish a connection with NVIDIA Omniverse.
Proceed as follows:
• Start Plant Simulation 2606 and open the Frame containing the simulation model, which you want to
use for exporting usd files or for a live connection with Omniverse.
• Change to the Edit ribbon tab and click Omniverse Connector 
 .
• This opens the LiveConnect window.
Back to Visualize the Simulation Model in Omniverse
Start the Omniverse Connector
10-1158 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Set Up a New Filesystem Connection
Set up a New Filesystem connection to export usd files and then establish a connection with Omniverse.
Proceed as follows:
• Click the Omniverse node in the LiveConnect window and select New Filesystem connection.
• Create a new folder in the file system on your computer by clicking the Make New Folder button or
select an existing folder in the File Browser. Our folder is named USD Data Files.
• Type a Description of the project into the dialog Add new Filesystem connection.
The LiveConnect window then shows our connection node.
Set Up a New Filesystem Connection
Plant Simulation Help 10-1159
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

 
• Click the USD Data Files folder and select Connect to establish the Omniverse connection with this
folder. Then, select the data folder link. Once the folder is selected, you can type a file name into the text
box File name at the bottom of the LiveConnect window.
Plant Simulation does currently not use the setting Frames per second, you can leave this box empty.
Export the Simulation in USD Format
After setting-up the file system connection, you can export the running simulation to usd files. USD stands
for Universal Scene Description.
Proceed as follows:
• Click Export to make Omniverse create the required usd files within the configured data folder.
Start the simulation, which you want to record in Plant Simulation.
Stop the simulation after everything is recorded that you want to show.
• Click Export again to stop the usd recording,
• Plant Simulation creates a library folder and a usd file in the data folder.
• You can then open the exported simulation project in the Nvidia Omniverse Composer and visualize the
simulation model.
Back to Visualize the Simulation Model in Omniverse
Set Up a New Filesystem Connection
10-1160 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Establish a Live Connection to Omniverse
Establishes a live connection to Omniverse using the Omniverse Nucleus Server.
Proceed as follows:
• Make sure that the Omniverse Nucleus Server is started and running.
• Right-click the Omniverse node in the LiveConnect window and select New Nucleus connection.
• Type in a Description and the IP address or the server name of the computer on which Omniverse
Nucleus is installed.
Type in the Port number, which is configured for the Omniverse Nucleus Server. Click OK to close the
dialog.
• Right-click the newly created server node and select Connect on the context menu.
You will then see the Omniverse data folder on the server computer.
• Create a folder structure in Nvidia Omniverse Composer in the Projects folder .
Establish a Live Connection to Omniverse
Plant Simulation Help 10-1161
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• Right-click the Library folder in the project, MyProject01 in our example. Then select Set System root
folder on the context menu.
• Select the project folder and type a project name into the text box File name. We typed in
MyLiveProject01.
• Click Connect and start the simulation in the Frame containing your simulation model.
• Open the project in the Live data area of the Nvidia Omniverse Composer.
• Stop the simulation in Plant Simulation and then terminate the Live connection by clicking Connect in
the LiveConnect window.
Back to Visualize the Simulation Model in Omniverse
