Use Omniverse with the Function MVA_WriteUSD
Creates and activates a Nucleus Connection, or creates and activates a Filesystem Connection, or
terminates a Live Connection, or a Filesystem Connection via SimTalk.
Remarks
Before using MVA_WriteUSD, you
• Either have to load the Omniverse DLL via SimTalk with
loadLibrary(applicationHome + "PlantSimOmniverse.dll")
• Or you have to manually start the Omniverse connection by clicking Omniverse Connector 
  on
the Edit ribbon tab in Plant Simulation.
Type
Function
Syntax
MVA_WriteUSD("parameter string")
Create and Activate a Nucleus Connection
Specify these instructions to create and activate a Nucleus Connection with MVA_WriteUSD:
var system_root_path:string = "/Projects/My_Project01/Library"
var output_path:string = "omniverse://127.0.0.1:80/Projects/My_Project01/
myExport.live"
MVA_writeUSD(output_path+"?sysroot="+system_root_path)
Parameter
The parameter string specifies the project file path in the first section and the Omniverse system root
folder in the second section, which is to be used for the USD export or a live connection.
MVA_writeUSD(<project file path>?systemroot=<system root path>) 
Use Omniverse with the Function MVA_WriteUSD
Plant Simulation Help 10-1163
